---
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Stories from the Studio | TJ Murphy</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A running journal of paintings, the places behind them, and new work by TJ Murphy." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://tjm.art/blog/" />
    <link href="/fonts/fonts.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/site-header.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page-shell">
      <SiteHeader />
      <main class="container journal">
        <header class="journal-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow dark">Stories from the studio</p>
          <h1>A painting is a place to begin.</h1>
          <p>Notes about the paintings, travels, and people behind my work. New stories appear here when they go out on Nostr.</p>
        </header>
        <p id="journal-status" class="journal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking for the latest story…</p>
        <section id="journal-entries" class="journal-entries" aria-label="Stories">
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/3d-gallery-to-relay-gate/">From a One-Room Dungeon to Relay Gate</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-20">October 20, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/3d-gallery-to-relay-gate/" aria-label="Read From a One-Room Dungeon to Relay Gate">
            <img src="/display/3d-gallery-cover-start-120ddab553-960.webp" alt="The first view inside the TJM Gallery 3D dungeon: a dark stone hall lined with lit paintings, a hologram of TJ playing guitar on a platform, and the checkout gate" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>How my 3D gallery at tjm.art/play grew from a one-room dungeon into museums, easter eggs and a gallery for Chase Toole, and why it led me to Relay Gate, an open-source gallery tool on Nostr and Bitcoin.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/3d-gallery-to-relay-gate/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/finding-a-sound-bass-from-dad/">Finding a Sound, and a Bass from My Dad</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-19">October 19, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/finding-a-sound-bass-from-dad/" aria-label="Read Finding a Sound, and a Bass from My Dad">
            <img src="/display/tj-playing-bass-poster-705eba8130-960.webp" alt="TJ playing the cream Epiphone bass his dad gave him" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>I&#x27;m working toward looped trance and dubstep on live instruments with a Line 6 HX Stomp XL, a looper, and the bass my dad finally handed down to me.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/finding-a-sound-bass-from-dad/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/brass-plate-etching-friends-club/">How I Etched a Brass Plate with a Silhouette Cameo and Ferric Chloride</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-19">October 19, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/brass-plate-etching-friends-club/" aria-label="Read How I Etched a Brass Plate with a Silhouette Cameo and Ferric Chloride">
            <img src="/display/friends-club-brass-plate-finished-5c66cc5ab7-960.webp" alt="Finished Friends Club brass plate: the astronaut mascot in a raft with a dog and Billy Buff" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>How I etched a brass plate for Friends Club in Lillooet, BC: a vinyl mask cut on a Silhouette Cameo, twenty minutes in ferric chloride, and Alpha enamel wiped into the lines.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/brass-plate-etching-friends-club/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-19-2026/">Site update: Oct 19</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-19">October 19, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/site-update-oct-19-2026/" aria-label="Read Site update: Oct 19">
            <img src="/display/esperanza-hero-aba277665d-1134.webp" alt="Esperanza, a painting by TJ Murphy" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>A dated log of changes to tjm.art on October 19, 2026, around my brass plate and bass posts.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-19-2026/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-17-18-2026/">Site update: Oct 17–18</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-18">October 18, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/site-update-oct-17-18-2026/" aria-label="Read Site update: Oct 17–18">
            <img src="/display/esperanza-hero-aba277665d-1134.webp" alt="Esperanza, a painting by TJ Murphy" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>A dated log of changes to tjm.art between my weekly recap on October 17 and my brass plate etching post on October 19, 2026.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-17-18-2026/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/my-week-in-art-oct-11-17-2026/">A Dungeon, a Backpacking Trip, and Two Juried Shows: My Week in Art (Oct 11–17)</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-17">October 17, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/my-week-in-art-oct-11-17-2026/" aria-label="Read A Dungeon, a Backpacking Trip, and Two Juried Shows">
            <img src="https://img.tjm.art/play/share.jpg" alt="Inside the TJM Gallery 3D dungeon, with paintings on the walls and a hologram of TJ playing guitar" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>Two juried shows, the Strawberry Point Backpacking Trip series, a 3D dungeon gallery you can walk through, and more of the archive out in the open.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/my-week-in-art-oct-11-17-2026/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-4-16-2026/">Site update: Oct 4–16</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-16">October 16, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/site-update-oct-4-16-2026/" aria-label="Read Site update: Oct 4–16">
            <img src="/display/esperanza-hero-aba277665d-1134.webp" alt="Esperanza, a painting by TJ Murphy" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>A dated log of changes to tjm.art between my Warsaw travel story on October 4 and my weekly recap on October 17, 2026.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/site-update-oct-4-16-2026/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/bitcoin-film-festival/">Coined in Watercolor: Warsaw, Kraków, and Prague</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-04">October 4, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/bitcoin-film-festival/" aria-label="Read Coined in Watercolor: Warsaw, Kraków, and Prague">
            <img src="https://media.vermillionaurora.com/images/blog/bitcoin-film-festival/005.jpg" alt="The finished Coined in Watercolor poster, painted for the Warsaw Film Festival" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>Three paintings made for Warsaw, Polish phrases, street sketches, a lively artists’ community, and a train ride through Kraków on the way to Prague.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/bitcoin-film-festival/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-entry" data-static-story>
          <header>
            <h2><a href="/blog/how-tjm-art-was-built/">How tjm.art was built</a></h2>
            <time datetime="2026-10-03">October 3, 2026</time>
          </header>
          <a class="journal-image-link" href="/blog/how-tjm-art-was-built/" aria-label="Read How tjm.art was built">
            <img src="/display/esperanza-hero-aba277665d-1134.webp" alt="Esperanza, a painting by TJ Murphy" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="journal-copy">
            <p>A dated log of how I built my art website, from the first commit in September 2026 to my first blog post on October 4, 2026.</p>
            <p><a href="/blog/how-tjm-art-was-built/">Read the story →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        </section>
      </main>
      <SiteFooter />
    </div>
    <script is:inline>
      const statusNode = document.getElementById('journal-status');
      const entriesNode = document.getElementById('journal-entries');
      const feedUrl = 'https://vermillion-nostr-publisher.timothyjosephmurphy.workers.dev/blog';

      function makeEntry(post) {
        const article = document.createElement('article');
        article.className = 'journal-entry';
        const header = document.createElement('header');
        const title = document.createElement('h2');
        title.textContent = post.title;
        const date = document.createElement('time');
        date.dateTime = post.publishedAt;
        date.textContent = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { dateStyle: 'long' }).format(new Date(post.publishedAt));
        header.append(title, date);
        const imageLink = document.createElement('a');
        imageLink.className = 'journal-image-link';
        imageLink.href = post.productUrl || post.imageUrl;
        imageLink.setAttribute('aria-label', 'View ' + post.title);
        const image = document.createElement('img');
        image.src = post.imageUrl;
        image.alt = post.title;
        image.loading = 'lazy';
        image.decoding = 'async';
        imageLink.append(image);
        const story = document.createElement('div');
        story.className = 'journal-copy';
        // Compact card: a short description only; the full text lives on the painting page / Nostr note.
        const firstParagraph = (post.text.split(/\n\s*\n/).find(Boolean) || '').trim();
        const summary = document.createElement('p');
        summary.textContent = firstParagraph.length > 180 ? firstParagraph.slice(0, 177).replace(/\s+\S*$/, '') + '…' : firstParagraph;
        story.append(summary);
        const links = document.createElement('div');
        links.className = 'journal-links';
        const product = document.createElement('a');
        product.href = post.productUrl;
        product.textContent = 'View this painting →';
        links.append(product);
        if (post.noteUrl) {
          const note = document.createElement('a');
          note.href = post.noteUrl;
          note.target = '_blank';
          note.rel = 'noopener noreferrer';
          note.textContent = 'Read the Nostr post ↗';
          links.append(note);
        }
        article.append(header, imageLink, story, links);
        return article;
      }

      fetch(feedUrl, { headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } })
        .then(response => {
          if (!response.ok) throw new Error('feed unavailable');
          return response.json();
        })
        .then(data => {
          const stories = Array.isArray(data.posts) ? data.posts : [];
          const staticStories = Array.from(entriesNode.querySelectorAll('[data-static-story]'));
          // Newest first, mixing the hand-written stories with Nostr posts.
          const dated = [
            ...staticStories.map(node => ({ node, time: Date.parse(node.querySelector('time')?.getAttribute('datetime') || '') || 0 })),
            ...stories.map(post => ({ node: makeEntry(post), time: Date.parse(post.publishedAt) || 0 })),
          ].sort((a, b) => b.time - a.time);
          entriesNode.replaceChildren(...dated.map(entry => entry.node));
          statusNode.textContent = stories.length || staticStories.length ? '' : 'The first story will appear here when it is released on Nostr.';
        })
        .catch(() => {
          statusNode.textContent = entriesNode.querySelector('[data-static-story]') ? '' : 'The story feed is temporarily unavailable. Please check back shortly.';
        });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
<style is:global>
  /* Compact story cards for every post, static and Nostr (studio-tracker #217): about three per screen. */
  .journal{max-width:980px;padding-block:32px 64px}
  .journal-heading{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 24px;text-align:center}
  .journal-heading .eyebrow{margin:0 0 10px}
  .journal-heading h1{font:600 clamp(2.3rem,5vw,4rem)/1.04 "Cormorant Garamond",serif;margin:0 0 12px}
  .journal-heading>p:last-child{max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}
  .journal-status{min-height:1.5em;text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
  .journal-entries{display:grid;gap:14px}
  .journal-entry{display:grid;grid-template-columns:260px minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:auto auto 1fr;gap:6px 22px;align-items:start;padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--line,#e3d9cb);border-radius:10px;background:#fffcf6}
  .journal-entry>header{grid-column:2;display:grid;gap:2px}
  .journal-entry h2{font:600 1.55rem/1.15 "Cormorant Garamond",serif;margin:0}
  .journal-entry h2 a{text-decoration:none}
  .journal-entry time{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}
  .journal-image-link{grid-column:1;grid-row:1 / span 3;display:block;height:165px;background:#eee7dd;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden}
  .journal-image-link img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}
  .journal-copy{grid-column:2;font-size:.93rem;line-height:1.5}
  .journal-copy p{margin:0 0 6px}
  .journal-copy p:first-child{display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
  .journal-links{grid-column:2;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;font-size:.88rem}
  .journal-links a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}
  @media(max-width:680px){
    .journal{padding-block:20px 48px}
    .journal-entry{grid-template-columns:96px minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:auto auto;gap:6px 12px;padding:10px}
    .journal-image-link{grid-row:1;height:96px}
    .journal-entry h2{font-size:1.15rem}
    .journal-copy,.journal-links{grid-column:1 / -1;font-size:.85rem}
    .journal-copy p:first-child{-webkit-line-clamp:2}
  }
</style>
